  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA (descriptive, verb-disciplined) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>US CENTCOM struck approximately 100 IRGC targets on September 1, including air defense sites, radar arrays, mine-laying vessels, anti-ship missile launchers, and for the first time two Iranian government tankers under an emerging "tanker-for-tanker" doctrine. Iranian authorities reported 18 killed including civilians at a wedding in Sirik county (Al Jazeera, Sep 1). Iran answered the same day with approximately 25 ballistic missiles at US military bases in Jordan and Kuwait, and two dozen drones at Bahrain; US officials reported no American casualties. → moved <span class="cite">F6</span></p>
      <p>Trump responded to Iran's Sep 2 retaliation by publicly refusing any negotiated deal: "We are done talking. Iran will be hit far harder if it tries that again." US halted envoy contacts August 18 after the June 17 Islamabad memorandum expired unextended on August 17. Iran's President Pezeshkian publicly offered to reciprocate a US return to the MOU framework, but the offer remained unanswered by both Washington and Iran's own military establishment. → supports <span class="cite">F3</span> without move</p>
      <p>Hormuz commercial traffic was recorded at approximately 8 vessels per day as of September 4 per Straits.live, representing roughly 5.8% of pre-war normal (138 vessels/day). CENTCOM stated the September 1 strikes against IRGC mine-laying capability had "bought at least a month" of lowered threat levels to commercial shipping; no named insurer has reinstated Hormuz war-risk cover as of September 4. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span></p>
      <p>Israeli election polls published around September 3 (Channel 13, Jerusalem Post) showed Yashar at 26 seats and Likud at 22 seats, with Eisenkot leading Netanyahu in PM preference by 14 percentage points (49% to 38%). A separate Haaretz poll (Aug 6) had placed the parties closer (23–22) but also with Yashar ahead. The right-wing coalition bloc tracked at 48–52 seats, well below the 61-seat governing threshold. → moved <span class="cite">F5</span></p>
      <p>Putin met Iran's President Pezeshkian in Bishkek on the sidelines of an SCO summit in early September; the Russian president described the June ceasefire as "too fragile" and Iran characterized the bilateral relationship as "strategic." No Russian mediation offer was announced at the meeting. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

